\begin{theorem}[Passive cost]\label{prop:passive}
Suppose the price is observed passively as the stationary output $x_t=H_\theta(L)\xi_t$ of i.i.d.\ Gaussian innovations $\xi_t\sim N(0,\sigma^2)$, $\sigma^2>0$ known, without observation noise, for $\theta$ in a compact, uniformly Schur-stable family with rates in $[\eta_{\min},\eta_{\max}]\subset(0,1)$, and let $D(\theta_1\|\theta_0)$ be the Kullback--Leibler divergence rate per observation.
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item For a single cohort at $\bar\eta$ against the symmetric pair at $\bar\eta\pm\delta$ with the same total weight, $D=\Theta(\delta^4)$.
\item For the moment-matched two-cohort economies of Theorem~\ref{thm:twocohort}, $D=\Theta(\tau^2(\Delta\eta)^6)$.
\item For every $K\ge2$, for the $K$-cohort Gauss and Gauss--Radau economies of Theorem~\ref{thm:kcohort}, $D=\Theta((\Delta\eta)^{4K-2})$.
\end{enumerate}
Hence any test based on $T$ passive observations with worst-case error at most $\alpha<1/4$ needs $T=\Omega(\delta^{-4})$, $T=\Omega(\tau^{-2}(\Delta\eta)^{-6})$ and $T=\Omega((\Delta\eta)^{-(4K-2)})$ respectively, uniformly as the separation shrinks: passive data cost at least the same polynomial order as active probing for every number of cohorts. For each fixed pair, at fixed type-I error the likelihood-ratio test's type-II error decays at exponential rate $D$ (Stein's lemma), and both errors decay at the Chernoff-information rate, which is of the same order in the separation; so the orders are the right ones; we do not claim that this attainment is uniform as the separation shrinks.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proposition}[Tagged flow removes the barrier]\label{prop:tagged}
Let the price be driven by i.i.d.\ innovations of variance $\sigma_\xi^2$ in a positive, stable economy, with stationary autocovariances $\gamma_x(s)=\sum_\ell c_\ell\lambda_\ell^{|s|}$ ($c_\ell\ge0$, $0\le\lambda_\ell<1$ the closed-loop modes). Suppose cohort $i$ has merged weight $w_i>0$ and the observer receives prices and each cohort's flow $\tilde u_{i,t}=u_{i,t}+\varepsilon_{i,t}$, $u_{i,t}=q_iy_{i,t}$, with i.i.d.\ measurement noise of variance $\sigma_f^2$ independent of prices. Then $\tilde u_{i,t}=r_i\tilde u_{i,t-1}+w_ix_t+e_{i,t}$ with $e_{i,t}=\varepsilon_{i,t}-r_i\varepsilon_{i,t-1}$, and the just-identified IV estimator of $\beta_i=(r_i,w_i)$ with instruments $Z_t=(x_{t-1},x_t)^\top$ satisfies $\sqrt T(\hat\beta_i-\beta_i)\to N(0,V_i)$,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:ivvar}
V_i=\Sigma_i^{-1}\Omega_i\Sigma_i^{-\top},\qquad \Sigma_i=\begin{pmatrix}w_iA_0&\gamma_x(1)\\ w_iA_1&\gamma_x(0)\end{pmatrix},\qquad \Omega_i=\sigma_f^2\bigl[(1+r_i^2)\Gamma_0-r_i(\Gamma_1+\Gamma_1^\top)\bigr],
\end{equation}
where $A_m=\sum_{s\ge0}r_i^s\gamma_x(s+m)$, $\Gamma_0=\begin{psmallmatrix}\gamma_x(0)&\gamma_x(1)\\ \gamma_x(1)&\gamma_x(0)\end{psmallmatrix}$ and $\Gamma_1=\E[Z_tZ_{t-1}^\top]$. The Jacobian determinant is
\begin{equation}\label{eq:ivdet}
\det\Sigma_i=w_i\sum_{\ell,m}c_\ell c_m\frac{1-\lambda_\ell\lambda_m}{1-r_i\lambda_m}\;>\;0 .
\end{equation}
$V_i$ depends only on cohort $i$'s own $(w_i,r_i)$, $\sigma_f^2$ and the price autocovariances, which are bounded and nondegenerate uniformly on a uniformly stable family with merged weights bounded below, whatever the rate spacing; so the merged weights are estimated at rate $T^{-1/2}$ with a constant that does not depend on $|r_i-r_j|$.
\end{proposition}

historical_types.p1_prop_tagged_flow_removes_barrier:
∀ (r_i w_i x_t u_prev sigma_f Var_x : ℝ),
  0 < sigma_f →
    0 < Var_x →
      have u_next := r_i * u_prev + w_i * x_t;
      have fisher_w_i := Var_x / sigma_f ^ 2;
      u_next - r_i * u_prev = w_i * x_t ∧ 0 < fisher_w_i

